# The openEMS toolchain's Python packages (issue #1). Lock with
# `bazel run //tools:requirements.update`; it writes requirements_lock.txt
# with every wheel's hash. PyPI has no CSXCAD or openEMS; their wheels are
# built once (tools/openems_wheels) and mirrored (tools/mirror/README.md).
csxcad @ https://github.com/filmil/bazel_rules_em/releases/download/mirror-openems-d686f1d/csxcad-0.7.0.post20261021-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_27_x86_64.manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
openems @ https://github.com/filmil/bazel_rules_em/releases/download/mirror-openems-d686f1d/openems-0.37.0.post20261024-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_27_x86_64.manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
# Their runtime dependencies (CSXCAD's and openEMS's pyproject.toml).
numpy
h5py
matplotlib
